<title>CHILE: Chile's Collahuasi names new CEO.</title>
<headline>Chile's Collahuasi names new CEO.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper project Collahuasi named engineer Diego Hernandez as its new general manager and executive president, replacing Steve Kessler who resigned earlier this year.</p>
<p>Hernandez until now has been general manager of copper mine Mantos Blancos, said Compania Minera Dona Ines de Collahuasi in a statement.</p>
<p>Collahuasi, one of the world's largest copper projects now being built, is owned 44 percent each by Falconbridge and Minorco and 12 percent by a Japanese consortium led by Mitsui &amp; Co. When finished in late 1998, it will produce about 300,000 tonnes of copper a year.</p>
<p>-- Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
